=A local business was checked from {{ $json.point_count }} points on a grid around it, searching for "{{ $json.keyword }}".

Business: {{ $json.business }}
It appeared in the local pack at {{ $json.in_pack }} of {{ $json.point_count }} points ({{ $json.coverage_pct }}%), average position {{ $json.avg_rank }}.

The map, north at the top. A number is the position in the pack at that point, a dash means it did not appear there, and the square in brackets is the business's own location:

{{ $json.map }}

Competitors appearing above it, and at how many of the points:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.rivals) }}

Write exactly two sentences for the business owner. The first says where on the map they are strong and where they are weak, using compass directions read off the grid. The second names the competitor that costs them the most and says at how many points. Plain language, no advice, no preamble, no bullet points. If they appear at every point, say so instead of inventing a weakness.

